description:
I don't believe we actually require RCurl, readr, or knitr.

@javierluraschi I don't believe we need anything other than devtools. Is that correct as far as you understand it? (@kevinushey might know of some reason to have RCurl?). Also, I realize we are keeping the list of GITHUB packages in there as a failsafe for now, just want to make sure that that code isn't executing (from looking at the source I don't believe it is but just want to confirm).

I would actually be in favor of removing the non-packrat branch entirely as it ultimately simply won't work for us to cherry-pick a set of package versions to pre-install. The only 2 viable scenarios are using packrat and allowing the user to provide an `install.R` script which does manual installation of dependencies. I'd rather we remove the old code and if packrat ends up being problematic for any reason we can introduce `install.R` as an alternative scheme.
